# What the installed app's own Python needs (made on first run by the setup screen, see src-tauri/src/runtime.rs).
# Edit this file (not the .txt), then regenerate both pinned lists from this folder:
#   uv pip compile requirements-runtime.in -o requirements-runtime.txt --python-version 3.12 --python-platform windows
#   uv pip compile requirements-test.in -o requirements-test.txt --python-version 3.12 --python-platform windows
# Add --upgrade to move every pin to its newest version.
# requirements.txt is the developer set; it also lists diffusers/transformers/accelerate for the optional AI outpaint of the
# local attraction-clip fallback, which needs PyTorch (several GB). Without them that fallback pans over the plain photo.
numpy
pandas
pyproj
contextily
scipy
Pillow
pillow-heif
opencv-python
httpx
requests
websocket-client
ollama
pydantic
deep-translator
pykakasi
tqdm
pydeck
playwright
python-dotenv
psutil
fugashi
unidic-lite
pypdf
rapidocr-onnxruntime
# Hears each narration line back to check place names (services/tts/name_check.py); CPU, int8.
faster-whisper
